## Context

PR #771 (ticket 0446) extended `src/aedist/plot_exp1_matrix.py`:
`write_pdf()` gained `models` / `exclude_models` filtering, `lang` (en|fr)
band labels, `page_aspect`, and a band-collision / leader-line layout loop;
`main()` gained `--models`, `--exclude-models`, `--lang`, `--page-aspect`.

The only existing smoke test (`test_plot_writes_nonempty_pdf`) calls
`write_pdf` with defaults, exercising none of these paths. Both
`/verify-adherence` and `/review-pr` flagged this as a coding-python.md
"changed behavior starts with a test" gap. It was dispositioned
non-blocking at merge because the render.mk rules that produce the
`_fr` / `_strong` / `_top` PDFs exercise the new flags and render clean —
but the rule still requires a committed test.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A test exercises `write_pdf` with `lang="fr"`, with `exclude_models=[...]`,
      and with `models=[...]` — each producing a non-empty PDF
- [ ] Marked `@pytest.mark.slow` if it needs the full fixture/render path
- [ ] `make check-fast` + `pytest -m adherence` green

## Suggested test (from /verify-adherence)

    @pytest.mark.slow
    def test_plot_subset_and_lang(fixture_dir, tmp_path):
        from aedist.plot_exp1_matrix import write_pdf
        glob, ref = fixture_dir
        out_fr = tmp_path / "fr.pdf"
        write_pdf(records_glob=glob, reference_path=ref, output=out_fr, lang="fr")
        assert out_fr.stat().st_size > 0
        out_x = tmp_path / "x.pdf"
        write_pdf(records_glob=glob, reference_path=ref, output=out_x,
                  exclude_models=["m2"])
        assert out_x.stat().st_size > 0
        out_i = tmp_path / "i.pdf"
        write_pdf(records_glob=glob, reference_path=ref, output=out_i,
                  models=["m1"])
        assert out_i.stat().st_size > 0

